+`family_id` is `lf-<smallest dataset_hash of the cluster>`. `evidence` is
+`name` when another table shares the (non-generic) canonical stem, `content`
+when the table joined its cluster through content links only, else `singleton`.
+Content evidence: a column (features and target) with more than 16 distinct
+finite values, rounded to 6 significant digits, is summarised by the 64
+smallest value hashes; two columns match when the bottom-k Jaccard estimate is
+>= 1/2; two tables are linked when at least 3 columns match in both directions
+and the matched columns are at least half of the eligible columns of the table
+with fewer of them (`--content-share smaller`, the default) or of each table
+(`--content-share each`). The choice is recorded in `overlap_report.json`
+(`rule.content_share`) and must be frozen with the panel.
