+Precisely: `G` is the number of duplicate groups of the table and `round` is
+half-up. The clamp applies when `G >= 600` (so A and B can still hold 200
+groups each); below that `n_T = round(0.30 * G)`. All sizes are in duplicate
+groups; a role holds every row of its groups, then A and B are thinned by
+seeded row sampling to the same row count (at most 1024) and C to at most that
+count. `stratum` is `headline` iff A, B and T each hold at least 200 duplicate
+groups after thinning (equal to row counts for a table without duplicate
+rows). The u64 seed of a stream is the first 8 bytes of the digest,
+little-endian; the split (`purpose = "split"`) and column (`"cols"`) streams
+use `sample_seed = 0`. Both views of a table share the row roles of their data
+seed. Tiers (data seeds x sample seeds, seeds numbered from 0): `lite` 1x1 on
+one table per family (most rows, ties to the smaller `dataset_hash`), `full`
+2x2, `confirm` 3x2, `sealed` 3x3 on every table.
